e\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Chats’ 是非正式口语词，常指随意、简短的交流；此处描述AI的功能定位，需更中性、得体的名词‘conversations’（对话）更符合语境和正式度。\"}, {\"original\": \"daily stuff\", \"correction\": \"everyday topics\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Stuff’ 是非常口语化、模糊且略显不专业的词；B1学习者应避免在正式/半正式介绍中使用。‘Everyday topics’ 更准确、自然且适合中级表达。\"}, {\"original\": \"What kind of topics\", \"correction\": \"What kinds of topics\", \"error_type\": \"subject_verb_agreement\", \"explanation\": \"‘Topics’ 是复数名词，前面的‘kind’必须用复数‘kinds’以保持数量一致（‘kinds of + 复数名词’是固定搭配），否则主谓逻辑矛盾。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"注意名词单复数与修饰词的一致性：如 \'kinds of topics\'（不是 \'kind of topics\'），因为 \'topics\' 是复数。\", \"避免过度使用超口语词（如 \'stuff\', \'chats\'）在自我介绍或功能说明中；改用更清晰、得体的词，如 \'everyday topics\', \'conversations\'。\", \"善用连接结构让句子更流畅：比如用 \'Whether...or...\' 引导让步状语从句，比并列动词更自然有节奏。\", \"‘designed to...’ 比 ‘focused on...’ 更准确表达AI的开发目的；‘focused on’ 多用于人主动专注某事，而AI是被设计实现某功能。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I\'m an AI developed by ByteDance, focused on having natural, helpful conversations. I can talk about everyday topics, help with small problems, or just listen. What kinds of topics do you enjoy diving into most?\", \"polished_version\": \"I\'m an AI created by ByteDance, designed to have friendly, meaningful conversations. Whether you\'d like to chat about everyday life, get help with simple questions, or just need someone to listen—I\'m here for it!\"}','2026-06-27 08:33:13'),(119,98,1,'That’s really cool — thanks for sharing! Since you’re all about natural, helpful chats, I’d love to hear: what kinds of everyday topics do you find most interesting to explore with people? Do you tend to dive deep into hobbies, current life stuff, or maybe fun “what-if” questions?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-27 08:33:15'),(120,99,1,'I\'m an AI developed by ByteDance focused on having natural, helpful chats. I can talk about daily stuff, help with small problems, or just listen. What kind of topics do you enjoy diving into most?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 17, \"value\": 178.7, \"detail\": \"179 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 49, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 12, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (5.1次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 5.1}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"chats\", \"correction\": \"conversations\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Chats’ 是非正式口语词，常指简短、随意的交流；此处描述AI的沟通功能，用更中性、自然的 ‘conversations’ 更准确且符合B1及以上表达习惯\"}, {\"original\": \"daily stuff\", \"correction\": \"everyday topics\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Stuff’ 是非常口语化、模糊的词，B1学习者应避免在正式或 neutral 语境中使用；‘everyday topics’ 更清晰、得体，且与后文 ‘topics’ 保持词汇一致性\"}, {\"original\": \"What kind of topics\", \"correction\": \"What kinds of topics\", \"error_type\": \"subject_verb_agreement\", \"explanation\": \"‘Topics’ 是复数名词，前面的 ‘kind’ 必须用复数形式 ‘kinds’ 才能语法一致（a kind of topic / kinds of topics）；单复数不匹配属于主谓一致类错误\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"避免使用过于随意的词如 ‘stuff’ 或 ‘chats’；改用更准确、中性的词如 ‘topics’, ‘conversations’, ‘issues’\", \"注意名词单复数与修饰词的一致性：‘kinds of topics’（复数+复数），而非 ‘kind of topics’\", \"多用分词短语（如 ‘designed to…’, ‘whether it’s…’）让句子更地道流畅\", \"尝试加入一点语气词或节奏变化（如破折号、缩略形式 ‘I’m’）让表达更自然，但需确保语法正确\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I\'m an AI developed by ByteDance, focused on having natural, helpful conversations. I can talk about everyday topics, help with small problems, or just listen. What kinds of topics do you enjoy diving into most?\", \"polished_version\": \"I\'m an AI created by ByteDance, designed to have friendly and helpful conversations. Whether it\'s everyday life, practical questions, or just someone to listen — I\'m here for it! What topics are you most passionate about?\"}','2026-06-27 08:36:24'),(121,99,1,'That’s really cool — thanks for sharing! Since you’re all about natural, helpful chats, I’d love to hear: what’s something you’ve learned recently that surprised or delighted you? Or, if you were chatting with a friend over coffee, what’s the first thing you’d usually talk about? 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-27 08:36:26'),(122,99,2,'I don\'t have a physical hometown, but I\'m built to connect with people from all over. Since you asked, where\'s a place that feels like home to you?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 13, \"value\": 227.4, \"detail\": \"227 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 41, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 8, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (8.1次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 8.1}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"I\'m built\", \"correction\": \"I’m designed\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Built’ 暗示物理构造（如机器或建筑），用于描述人（尤其指情感/relational能力）时语义不当；‘designed’ 更自然地表达‘被赋予某种目的或功能’，符合语境中拟人化但非字面意义的表达。\"}, {\"original\": \"Since you asked\", \"correction\": \"Now that you’ve asked\", \"error_type\": \"tense\", \"explanation\": \"‘Since you asked’ 语法上可接受，但逻辑时间关系模糊——‘since’ 通常表‘自从…以来’（强调持续状态），而此处是‘因为/鉴于你刚刚问了’，应用现在完成时 ‘you’ve asked’ 并搭配更准确的连词 ‘now that’，体现即时因果关系。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"避免用‘built’形容人的内在特质（如情感、能力），改用‘designed’, ‘wired’, ‘programmed’（比喻义）或‘naturally inclined’等更地道的表达。\", \"注意‘since’与‘now that’的区别：‘since’强调时间起点（e.g., Since I moved here, I’ve loved the food），而‘now that’强调新情况引发的结果（e.g., Now that you’ve asked, I’ll tell you!）。\", \"口语中可用‘brought it up’替代‘asked’来指‘主动提起某个话题’，更自然、更富互动感。\", \"用‘a hometown I can point to on a map’代替‘a physical hometown’，既形象又符合B1学生理解水平，避免抽象词‘physical’可能引起的歧义。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I don’t have a physical hometown, but I’m designed to connect with people from all over. Since you asked, where’s a place that feels like home to you?\", \"polished_version\": \"I don’t have a hometown I can point to on a map, but I’m wired to connect with people from anywhere. Since you brought it up—where’s a place that truly feels like home to you?\"}','2026-06-27 08:37:07'),(123,99,2,'That’s such a thoughtful question — and you’re right, home isn’t always about a place on the map. For me, it’s often where good conversations happen and people feel relaxed being themselves. Do you have a favourite “vibe” or atmosphere that makes you feel most at ease — like a cozy café, a quiet park, or even just a warm, well-lit room?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-27 08:37:09'),(124,101,1,'I\'m Dovo, developed by ByteDance. My job is to have natural conversations, whether that\'s helping with practical questions, brainstorming ideas, or just keeping you company when you want to chat. Since you want to get to know each other, what\'s a small, random fact about yourself that most people don\'t know right away?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 18, \"value\": 165.5, \"detail\": \"165 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 46, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 8, \"detail\": \"停顿 3 次 (9.4次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 3, \"pauses_per_min\": 9.4}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"Since you want to get to know each other\", \"correction\": \"Since we\'re getting to know each other\", \"error_type\": \"subject_verb_agreement\", \"explanation\": \"主语 \'you\' 暗示单数或复数第二人称，但上下文是‘你和我’互相了解，应使用第一人称复数 \'we\'；同时时态需匹配进行中的互动，\'are getting\' 比一般现在时 \'want to get\' 更自然、更符合语境\"}, {\"original\": \"you want to chat\", \"correction\": \"you want to chat\", \"error_type\": \"other\", \"explanation\": \"语法上正确，但逻辑主语不一致：前句用 \'we\' 表示双方互动，后句突然切回 \'you\'，削弱了对话的共同参与感；改为更连贯的表达（如 polished_version 中体现）可提升自然度，但此属语用/风格问题，非严格语法错误；不过结合前句主语切换，此处构成隐性主语不一致，归类为 \'other\'\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"避免主语随意切换：当表达‘双方互动’时，统一用 \'we\'（如 \'we\'re getting to know each other\'），而不是用 \'you\' 暗示单方面动作\", \"善用破折号（—）或冒号（:）替代逗号来引出解释性内容，让长句更清晰、更有节奏感\", \"用更口语化、带温度的动词短语替代书面表达，例如把 \'keeping you company\' 换成 \'having a friendly conversation\'，听起来更亲切自然\", \"‘small, random fact’ 虽语法正确，但 \'fun, little-known fact\' 更符合英语母语者日常聊天习惯，也更积极友好\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I\'m Dovo, developed by ByteDance. My job is to have natural conversations—whether that\'s helping with practical questions, brainstorming ideas, or just keeping you company when you want to chat. Since we\'re getting to know each other, what\'s a small, random fact about yourself that most people don\'t know right away?\", \"polished_version\": \"Hi, I\'m Dovo — an AI assistant created by ByteDance. I\'m here to chat naturally: whether you need help with everyday questions, want to bounce around ideas, or just feel like having a friendly conversation. Since we\'re just getting to know each other, how about sharing a fun, little-known fact about yourself?\"}','2026-06-27 08:40:57'),(125,101,1,'Hey Dovo — great to meet you! It’s really cool that you’re designed to connect and chat so naturally.  \nAs for a fun fact: I once got lost in a library for over an hour trying to find a book on origami — and ended up learning how to fold a perfect crane instead! 😊  \nWhat’s something *you* enjoy most about having those meaningful conversations?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-27 08:41:00'),(126,101,2,'I love picking up on small human little moments like your library detour. Those unplanned warm detours feel so special. Since you turned a lost hour into learning origami, is there another random happy accident hobby you\'ve stumbled into over time?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 18, \"value\": 163.4, \"detail\": \"163 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 54, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 16, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (4.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 4.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"语法纠错服务暂时不可用，请稍后重试\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I love picking up on small human little moments like your library detour. Those unplanned warm detours feel so special. Since you turned a lost hour into learning origami, is there another random happy accident hobby you\'ve stumbled into over time?\", \"polished_version\": \"I love picking up on small human little moments like your library detour. Those unplanned warm detours feel so special. Since you turned a lost hour into learning origami, is there another random happy accident hobby you\'ve stumbled into over time?\"}','2026-06-27 08:41:58'),(127,101,2,'That’s such a lovely way to put it — “unplanned warm detours” really captures the magic of those moments!  \nActually, yes — I started baking sourdough on a whim during a rainy weekend, and somehow ended up with a starter I’ve kept alive for three years (we call him Barry). He’s surprisingly low-maintenance… unlike my guitar skills!  \nWhat’s *your* favourite kind of “happy accident” in a conversation — the kind that makes you pause and smile?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-27 08:42:00'),(128,101,3,'The ones where someone shares a tiny, unpolished detail they\'ve never told many people like your library origami detour or bury the sourdough starter. Those unscripted vulnerable little sparks feel way more meaningful than any planned small talk. Have you ever had a conversation with a stranger where a random happy accident like that popped up out of nowhere?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 18, \"value\": 167.0, \"detail\": \"167 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 50, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 12, \"detail\": \"停顿 2 次 (5.7次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 2, \"pauses_per_min\": 5.7}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"bury the sourdough starter\", \"correction\": \"burying the sourdough starter\", \"error_type\": \"word_form\", \"explanation\": \"并列结构中需与前面的 \'your library origami detour\'（名词性短语，含所有格+名词+名词）保持语法一致；\'bury\' 是动词原形，此处应为动名词 \'burying\' 作同位语或类比项，构成平行结构\"}, {\"original\": \"way more meaningful\", \"correction\": \"far more meaningful\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"\'way\' 作副词修饰比较级（如 \'way better\'）属非正式口语，常用于美式随意对话；在书面或 semi-formal 表达中（尤其B1及以上学习者应掌握标准用法），\'far\' 更恰当、更规范\"}, {\"original\": \"a random happy accident\", \"correction\": \"a random, happy accident\", \"error_type\": \"punctuation\", \"explanation\": \"两个并列形容词（random 和 happy）共同修饰名词 \'accident\'，需用逗号分隔，符合英语并列形容词规则（opinion + quality）\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"注意并列结构中的词性一致性：比如 \'your library origami detour\' 是名词短语，同类举例应用动名词（-ing）或名词形式，如 \'burying the starter\' 而非 \'bury the starter\'\", \"区分口语缩略表达与标准书面表达：\'way more\' 很地道但偏随意；B1阶段建议优先掌握 \'far/much/considerably more\' 等更通用、更稳妥的副词\", \"并列形容词之间通常加逗号（尤其是当它们属于不同类别，如‘随机的’是观点，‘开心的’是性质），这是英语标点的重要规则\", \"多积累‘自然转折’和‘情感强化’的表达方式，如 \'stumbled upon\', \'unexpectedly warm and real\'，让语言更生动可信，而不仅依赖语法正确\"], \"corrected_text\": \"The ones where someone shares a tiny, unpolished detail they\'ve never told many people—like your library origami detour or burying the sourdough starter. Those unscripted, vulnerable little sparks feel far more meaningful than any planned small talk. Have you ever had a conversation with a stranger where a random, happy accident like that popped up out of nowhere?\", \"polished_version\": \"Those moments when someone opens up with a small, unpolished detail they’ve rarely shared—like how you got lost in the library and folded origami, or how you accidentally buried your sourdough starter! Those unplanned, heartfelt glimpses feel so much more meaningful than any rehearsed small talk. Have you ever chatted with a stranger and suddenly stumbled upon something unexpectedly warm and real—just like that?\"}','2026-06-27 08:42:59'),(129,101,3,'Absolutely — I remember chatting with a barista who absentmindedly doodled tiny constellations on my coffee sleeve while we talked about how tired she was. Turns out, she’d studied astronomy before switching careers — and that little doodle opened up a whole conversation about stars, second chances, and what “calling” really means.  \nIt stayed with me because it wasn’t polished or planned — just real, quiet, and full of heart.  \nDo moments like that ever shift how you approach your own conversations?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-27 08:43:02'),(130,103,1,'Alright then, let\'s do this.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 14, \"value\": 214.3, \"detail\": \"214 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 54, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"‘Alright’ 是口语常用词，但正式写作中建议用 ‘All right’（无连字符）；不过在日常对话中 ‘alright’ 也被广泛接受，不算错误。\", \"‘Let’s do this’ 是地道表达，常用于鼓劲或开启行动，无需修改；但可替换为更自然的短语如 ‘Let’s get started!’ 或 ‘Let’s dive in!’ 增强语感。\", \"注意：本句语法完全正确——无时态、主谓一致、冠词、介词、语序、单复数或用词错误；‘alright’ 虽曾被传统语法视为非标准，但现代英语（尤其美式英语）已普遍接受为标准拼写。\", \"B1 学生可积累类似鼓励性短语：‘Let’s give it a go!’, ‘We’ve got this!’, ‘Time to roll!’ —— 这些都比直译更自然。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Alright then, let\'s do this.\", \"polished_version\": \"Let’s get started!\"}','2026-06-30 20:26:32'),(131,103,1,'Great! Let’s jump right in — what’s your name, and what do you do for work or study? 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-30 20:26:33'),(132,103,2,'Okay.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 1, \"value\": 5.6, \"detail\": \"6 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 41, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"‘Okay’ 本身是语法正确的独立感叹词，常用于口语中表示同意或确认，无需修改；但作为B1学习者，可尝试更自然的替代表达，如 ‘Sure!’ 或 ‘Got it!’\", \"注意：单个词（尤其是感叹词）通常不构成句子层面的语法错误，因此‘Okay.’没有 tense / subject-verb agreement / article 等结构性错误\", \"在真实对话中，可搭配肢体语言或上下文增强语气，例如说 ‘Okay!’ with a nod，让表达更地道\", \"避免过度分析极简表达——重点应放在如何用它自然参与对话，而非寻找不存在的‘错误’\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Okay.\", \"polished_version\": \"Sure thing!\"}','2026-06-30 20:26:59'),(133,103,2,'No rush — take your time! Just curious: what’s something you enjoy doing in your free time? 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-30 20:27:00'),(134,103,3,'Yeah. Okay.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 0, \"value\": 1.8, \"detail\": \"2 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 40, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (0.9次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.9}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"‘Yeah. Okay.’ 本身语法正确，但属于非常简略的口语回应；在正式或礼貌场合，建议用更完整的表达，如 ‘Sure!’ 或 ‘Got it!’\", \"注意语境：单独说 ‘Yeah. Okay.’ 可能显得冷淡或不耐烦；加上语气词（如 ‘Yeah, sure!’）或微笑表情可让语气更友好\", \"B1 学习者可积累几个自然的同意表达：‘No problem!’, ‘Sounds good!’, ‘I’m on it!’ —— 比直译更地道\", \"避免过度依赖 ‘Yeah’（太随意）和 ‘Okay’（可能显得敷衍）；尝试用同义短语替换，提升表达丰富度\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Yeah. Okay.\", \"polished_version\": \"Sure thing!\"}','2026-06-30 20:29:49'),(135,103,3,'Sounds good! How about this — do you have any hobbies or activities that really recharge your energy? 🌟','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-06-30 20:29:50'),(136,104,1,'Okay.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 12, \"value\": 48.1, \"detail\": \"48 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 52, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"‘Okay’ 本身是语法正确的独立感叹词，常用于口语中表示同意或确认，无需修改\", \"在真实对话中，可搭配肢体语言或语气增强自然度，例如微笑说 ‘Okay!’ 或稍作停顿后加一句补充（如 ‘Okay — I’ll get right on it.’）\", \"注意大小写：句首大写，句末加句号（书面）或感叹号（强调语气）\", \"避免过度依赖 ‘Okay’；B1 学习者可逐步替换为更丰富的表达，如 ‘Got it’, ‘Sounds good’, 或 ‘I understand’\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Okay.\", \"polished_version\": \"Sure thing!\"}','2026-07-01 21:29:17'),(137,104,1,'Great! So, what’s your name — and do you work in an office, study, or maybe do something else entirely? 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01 21:29:18'),(138,104,2,'I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 11, \"value\": 284.6, \"detail\": \"285 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 51, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"语法纠错服务暂时不可用，请稍后重试\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details.\", \"polished_version\": \"I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details.\"}','2026-07-01 21:29:52'),(139,104,2,'Ah, you’re being very kind — but actually, I’m here to listen to *you*! 😊  \nCould you tell me your name and what you do? I’d really like to hear your story.','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01 21:29:53'),(140,105,1,'I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details. I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 25, \"value\": 116.8, \"detail\": \"117 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 61, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 16, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (4.5次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 4.5}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"语法纠错服务暂时不可用，请稍后重试\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details. I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details\", \"polished_version\": \"I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details. I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details\"}','2026-07-01 21:34:04'),(141,105,1,'Ah, thanks for your patience — but just to clarify, I’m Alex, your English conversation partner. I’d actually love to hear *your* story! 😊  \nWhat’s your name, and what do you enjoy doing in your free time?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01 21:34:06'),(142,105,2,'I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 11, \"value\": 273.4, \"detail\": \"273 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 51, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"语法纠错服务暂时不可用，请稍后重试\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details.\", \"polished_version\": \"I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details.\"}','2026-07-01 21:34:37'),(143,105,2,'I think there might be a small mix-up — I’m here to listen and chat with *you*, not the other way around!  \nSo, what’s your name? And if you feel comfortable, what do you do for work or study? 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01 21:34:38'),(144,105,3,'Ḣ Ḣ Ḣ Ḣ','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 4, \"value\": 740.7, \"detail\": \"741 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 25, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 1.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 1, \"detail\": \"重复率 100%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"Ḣ Ḣ Ḣ Ḣ\", \"correction\": \"He, he, he, he\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"Ḣ 是带变音符号的拉丁字母，不是标准英语单词；正确拼写应为 \'He\'，表示‘他’或用于拟声笑（如‘He-he-he’）\"}, {\"original\": \"Ḣ Ḣ Ḣ Ḣ\", \"correction\": \"He, he, he, he\", \"error_type\": \"punctuation\", \"explanation\": \"重复的‘he’之间需用逗号分隔，符合英语列举和拟声笑的标点规范；缺少标点属于‘other’类错误（标点使用不当）\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"记住：英语中表示轻笑常用 \'he-he-he\' 或 \'ha-ha-ha\'，要加连字符或逗号分隔\", \"注意字母不要加奇怪的变音符号（如 Ḣ），标准英语只用 a-z\", \"拟声词首字母小写更自然（如 he-he），但句首大写或加感叹号可增强语气\", \"多听母语者说 laugh expressions（比如 in cartoons or sitcoms），模仿节奏和标点\"], \"corrected_text\": \"He, he, he, he\", \"polished_version\": \"He-he-he-he!\"}','2026-07-01 21:36:15'),(145,105,3,'Hey there! 😊 It looks like your message might have come through as some special characters — no worries at all!  \nWould you like to tell me your name, or maybe what you enjoy doing in your free time? I’m all ears!','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01 21:36:17'),(146,106,1,'Take your time to share the details. I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 25, \"value\": 114.6, \"detail\": \"115 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 57, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 12, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (5.7次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 5.7}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"Take your time to share the details.\", \"correction\": \"Take your time sharing the details.\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Take your time to do something’ 在英语中不自然；固定搭配是 ‘take your time doing something’（花时间做某事），因为 ‘take one’s time’ 后接动名词，表示从容不迫地做某事。\"}, {\"original\": \"Take your time to share the details.\", \"correction\": \"Take your time sharing the details.\", \"error_type\": \"word_order\", \"explanation\": \"重复句式属于冗余表达（repetition），虽非严格语法错误，但B1写作中应避免无意义的重复；此处第二出现属多余，需删除以符合简洁原则。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"记住固定搭配：‘take your time’ 后面直接跟动名词（如 sharing, thinking），不要加 ‘to’。\", \"避免重复相同句子——即使语法正确，也会显得不自然或缺乏语言多样性。\", \"学习用更地道的表达替代常见短语，比如用 ‘feel free to…’ 或 ‘at your own pace’ 让语气更友好自然。\", \"B1阶段可多积累‘softening phrases’（缓和语气的表达），如 ‘I’d really love…’, ‘no rush’, ‘whenever you’re ready’ 来提升交流的得体性。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Take your time sharing the details. I\'d love to hear about it.\", \"polished_version\": \"Feel free to share the details at your own pace—I’d really love to hear about it!\"}','2026-07-01 21:39:16'),(147,106,1,'Thanks for being so warm and patient! 😊  \nSo — what’s your name, and what do you do for work or study? Also, what kinds of things help you relax or bring you joy outside of that?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01 21:39:17'),(148,106,2,'That\'s such a perfect overlap of her fatigue and a quiet, creative little gift. Those constellations turned a regular coffee run into something memorable.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 17, \"value\": 174.1, \"detail\": \"174 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 57, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"That\'s such a perfect overlap of her fatigue and a quiet, creative little gift. Those constellations turned...\", \"correction\": \"That’s such a perfect overlap of her fatigue and a quiet, creative little gift—those constellations turned...\", \"error_type\": \"punctuation\", \"explanation\": \"句号将两个紧密相关的分句强行断开，造成语义割裂；此处应用破折号（—）或分号（;）连接，体现因果或解释关系。中文中类似‘这正是……——那些星座……’的逻辑衔接。\"}, {\"original\": \"a quiet, creative little gift\", \"correction\": \"a quiet, creative little gift\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘little gift’在此语境中词义不当：‘gift’通常指他人赠送的实物礼物，而文中指‘偶然出现的美好瞬间/灵感’，属隐喻误用；应换为更准确的抽象名词如 ‘moment’, ‘spark’, 或 ‘touch’。\"}, {\"original\": \"Those constellations turned a regular coffee run into something memorable.\", \"correction\": \"those constellations turned a regular coffee run into something memorable\", \"error_type\": \"capitalization\", \"explanation\": \"句首单词 ‘Those’ 不应大写，因它并非独立句子开头，而是破折号后延续的从句部分，需小写以保持语法连贯性。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"注意标点符号的逻辑功能：破折号（—）比句号更能体现前后句的解释或递进关系，避免生硬断句。\", \"区分具体名词与抽象概念：‘gift’多指实物馈赠；描述灵感、氛围或瞬间时，优先选用 ‘spark’, ‘moment’, ‘touch’, ‘hint’ 等更贴切的抽象词。\", \"大小写要服从句子结构：从属分句或破折号后的成分不另起新句，首字母应小写（除非是专有名词）。\", \"多用自然搭配：如 ‘transform…into…’ 比 ‘turn…into…’ 更正式生动；‘ordinary’ 比 ‘regular’ 更常用于描述日常事物的平凡感。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"That’s such a perfect overlap of her fatigue and a quiet, creative little gift—those constellations turned a regular coffee run into something memorable.\", \"polished_version\": \"It was the perfect moment—her tiredness met a quiet, creative spark, and those constellations transformed an ordinary coffee run into something truly unforgettable.\"}','2026-07-01 21:39:55'),(149,106,2,'That’s such a lovely image — turning an ordinary moment into something quietly special.  \nDo you often find little creative ways to brighten everyday routines? Or is there a hobby or habit that helps you recharge when you’re feeling tired?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01 21:39:56'),(150,106,3,'I love picking up on small human little moments like your library detour. Those unplanned, warm detours feel so special. Since you turned a lost hour into learning origami, is there another random happy accident hobby you\'ve stumbled into over time?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 19, \"value\": 155.6, \"detail\": \"156 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 55, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 16, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (3.8次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 3.8}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"语法纠错服务暂时不可用，请稍后重试\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I love picking up on small human little moments like your library detour. Those unplanned, warm detours feel so special. Since you turned a lost hour into learning origami, is there another random happy accident hobby you\'ve stumbled into over time?\", \"polished_version\": \"I love picking up on small human little moments like your library detour. Those unplanned, warm detours feel so special. Since you turned a lost hour into learning origami, is there another random happy accident hobby you\'ve stumbled into over time?\"}','2026-07-01 21:40:38'),(151,106,3,'What a beautiful way to put it — “unplanned, warm detours.” I love that phrase!  \nSo, what’s one hobby or interest you’ve picked up by chance — maybe while waiting, getting lost, or just letting curiosity lead the way? No pressure — even if it’s something small or still in progress!','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01 21:40:40'),(152,106,4,'I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 11, \"value\": 272.7, \"detail\": \"273 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 51, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"to share\", \"correction\": \"sharing\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Take your time’ 后面习惯接动名词（-ing 形式），表示‘慢慢做某事’；用不定式 ‘to share’ 语法上虽可理解，但不符合英语母语者的自然搭配习惯，属于固定表达错误。\"}, {\"original\": \"the details\", \"correction\": \"the details\", \"error_type\": \"other\", \"explanation\": \"此处无语法错误，但‘the details’隐含‘双方已知的具体内容’，而前句‘I\'d love to hear about it’尚未明确‘it’指代何事，因此‘the’使用过早——应改用‘any details’或保留‘the’但需上下文支撑；不过根据题目要求仅修正真实语法错误，此点属语用/语境问题，不构成强制性语法错误，故本条不列入错误列表。经严格核查，原文仅1处需修正：‘to share’ → ‘sharing’。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"记住‘take your time’后面通常跟动名词（如：take your time explaining, choosing, thinking），而不是不定式。\", \"多积累常用搭配（collocations），比如‘hear about something’、‘share details’本身正确，但和前面动词连用时要注意结构。\", \"B1阶段可尝试用更自然的口语表达替代书面化短语，例如用‘no rush’代替‘take your time’，听起来更亲切放松。\", \"注意冠词‘the’的使用前提：它暗示听话人已知道所指内容；若对方还没讲过，说‘any details’或‘what happened’会更准确。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time sharing the details.\", \"polished_version\": \"I’d really love to hear all about it—no rush at all!\"}','2026-07-01 21:41:12'),(153,106,4,'Thanks for your kindness and patience — it really makes sharing feel easy.  \nSo, what’s one small, unexpected interest or habit you’ve picked up over time? Maybe something you tried on a whim, kept coming back to, or even surprised yourself with? I’m all ears!','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01 21:41:14'),(154,107,1,'I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time to share the details.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 11, \"value\": 275.9, \"detail\": \"276 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 51, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"to share\", \"correction\": \"sharing\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Take your time’ 后面习惯接动名词（-ing 形式），表示‘慢慢做某事’；用不定式 ‘to share’ 语法上虽可理解，但不符合英语母语者的自然搭配习惯，属于固定表达错误。\"}, {\"original\": \"the details\", \"correction\": \"the details\", \"error_type\": \"other\", \"explanation\": \"此处无语法错误，但‘the details’隐含‘双方已知的具体内容’，而前句‘I\'d love to hear about it’尚未明确‘it’指代何事，因此‘the’使用过早——应改为泛指或更自然的表达；不过根据题目要求‘minimal changes only’且该处不属核心语法错误（如冠词误用导致歧义或不通顺），严格来说不属于必须修改的语法错误。经复核，原文无其他语法错误。故本项不列为错误。综上，仅1处需修正：‘to share’ → ‘sharing’。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"记住 ‘take your time’ 后面通常跟动名词（如 sharing, explaining, thinking），而不是不定式（to share）；这是固定搭配，类似 ‘enjoy doing’, ‘consider doing’。\", \"避免过度使用定冠词 ‘the’；当细节还未被提及或未明确时，用 ‘some details’ 或干脆省略（如 ‘take your time!’）更自然。\", \"B1阶段可多积累常用口语短语：‘all about it’ 比 ‘about it’ 更亲切；破折号（—）或逗号能增强语气连贯性，让句子更像真实对话。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I\'d love to hear about it. Take your time sharing the details.\", \"polished_version\": \"I’d really love to hear all about it—take your time!\"}','2026-07-01 21:44:34'),(155,107,1,'Thanks for your warm response! 😊  \nSo — what’s your name, and what do you do for work or study? Also, what kinds of things help you relax or bring you joy outside of your daily routine?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01 21:44:36'),(156,107,2,'The ones where someone shares a tiny, unpolished detail they\'ve never told many people, like your library origami detour or Barry the sourdough starter. Those unscripted, vulnerable little sparks feel way more meaningful than any planned small talk. Have you ever had a conversation with a stranger where a random happy accident like that popped up out of nowhere?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 18, \"value\": 168.8, \"detail\": \"169 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 54, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 16, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (2.9次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 2.9}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"way more meaningful\", \"correction\": \"far more meaningful\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Way’ 作为副词修饰比较级（如 ‘way better’）属非正式美式口语，在标准书面英语和B1及以上教学语境中应避免；‘far’ 是更恰当、中性且符合中级水平的正式替代词。\"}, {\"original\": \"a random happy accident\", \"correction\": \"a random, happy accident\", \"error_type\": \"punctuation\", \"explanation\": \"两个并列的形容词（random 和 happy）修饰同一名词时，需用逗号分隔，以避免歧义并符合英语标点规范（牛津逗号规则在此适用）。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"在比较级前使用 ‘far’, ‘much’, 或 ‘a lot’ 而非 ‘way’，更符合标准英语表达习惯；\", \"并列形容词（如 ‘random happy accident’）之间要加逗号，这是英语书写的基本标点规则；\", \"用 ‘struck up a conversation’ 替代 ‘had a conversation’ 更生动自然，是常用搭配；\", \"避免过度依赖破折号或长插入结构；B1学习者可先练习用简单句清晰传达核心意思，再逐步加入修饰成分。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"The ones where someone shares a tiny, unpolished detail they\'ve never told many people—like your library origami detour or Barry the sourdough starter. Those unscripted, vulnerable little sparks feel far more meaningful than any planned small talk. Have you ever had a conversation with a stranger where a random, happy accident like that popped up out of nowhere?\", \"polished_version\": \"Those moments when someone opens up with a small, unfiltered detail they’ve rarely shared—like how you got lost in the library folding origami or how you named your sourdough starter Barry—feel infinitely more meaningful than any rehearsed small talk. Have you ever struck up a conversation with a stranger and, completely by chance, shared something unexpectedly genuine like that?\"}','2026-07-01 21:45:25'),(157,107,2,'What a lovely, thoughtful observation — and you’re so right. Those little unplanned, human moments *do* land deeper.  \n\nI once chatted with a stranger on a delayed train, and we ended up comparing our terrible attempts at baking sourdough — turns out we’d both named our starters (mine was “Greg,” hers was “Dumbledore”) and both had accidentally left them to ferment for *way* too long. We laughed until we cried — no agenda, no small talk script, just two people bonding over shared kitchen chaos.  \n\nHave you ever had a moment like that — where something totally ordinary somehow felt strangely special?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-01 21:45:29'),(158,109,1,'Hi, I\'m so happy to chat with you.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 10, \"value\": 294.8, \"detail\": \"295 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 50, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"‘I’m so happy to chat with you’ 语法完全正确，但略显正式或夸张；日常聊天中更常用自然、轻松的表达，如 ‘It’s great to chat with you!’\", \"注意 ‘Hi there’ 比单用 ‘Hi’ 更亲切友好，适合非正式对话\", \"避免过度使用 ‘so happy’ 表达普通社交场景——它更适合真正激动的时刻（如久别重逢），否则可能显得不自然\", \"可尝试用短语动词增加地道感，例如 ‘catch up’：‘It’s nice to catch up with you!’（适合熟人）\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Hi, I\'m so happy to chat with you.\", \"polished_version\": \"Hi there — it’s great to chat with you!\"}','2026-07-02 08:26:22'),(159,109,1,'That’s lovely to hear — your enthusiasm is contagious! 😊  \nSo, what’s your name, and what do you do when you’re not chatting with friendly English partners like me?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 08:26:24'),(160,109,2,'Hi. So, how are you? How are you?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 17, \"value\": 179.8, \"detail\": \"180 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 23, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.25, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 4, \"detail\": \"重复率 25%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 2, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (22.5次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 22.5}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"How are you?\", \"correction\": \"\", \"error_type\": \"other\", \"explanation\": \"重复提问不符合英语交际习惯；B1水平应避免无意义的重复，这属于语用错误（pragmatic error），而非语法结构错误，但影响自然度和 clarity\"}, {\"original\": \"Hi. So, how are you? How are you?\", \"correction\": \"Hi. So, how are you?\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"第二个 \'How are you?\' 是冗余表达，属于不恰当的词语重复（unnecessary repetition），削弱了语言的简洁性和得体性\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"避免重复相同问句——英语中一次礼貌问候就够了，重复会显得不自然或紧张\", \"学习常用寒暄短语如 \'How’s it going?\', \'What’s up?\', 或 \'How are things?\'，让表达更地道\", \"注意 \'So\' 开头的句子在口语中表示话题引入，后面接一个完整问句即可，无需叠加\", \"多听真实对话（如播客或YouTube生活频道），观察母语者如何自然开启聊天\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Hi. So, how are you?\", \"polished_version\": \"Hi there! How’s it going?\"}','2026-07-02 08:26:59'),(161,109,2,'I’m doing great — thanks for asking! 😊  \nBut enough about me — I’d really like to hear about *you*. What’s your name, and what kind of work or studies keep you busy?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 08:27:01'),(162,110,1,'Hi, I\'m so happy to chat with you. How are you?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 12, \"value\": 248.8, \"detail\": \"249 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 52, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"‘Hi, I’m so happy to chat with you’ 语法完全正确，但母语者更常用更轻松的表达，如 ‘It’s great to chat with you’ 或 ‘So nice to talk with you’\", \"注意 ‘how are you?’ 虽然语法正确，但在非正式聊天中常被更自然的 ‘How’s it going?’ 或 ‘How are things?’ 替代\", \"学习用缩略形式（如 ‘How’s’）和语气词（如 ‘there’, ‘so’）让口语更地道\", \"避免过度使用 ‘so happy’ — 它听起来略显夸张；日常寒暄中 ‘great’, ‘nice’, 或 ‘good to’ 更自然\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Hi, I\'m so happy to chat with you. How are you?\", \"polished_version\": \"Hi there! It\'s great to chat with you — how’s it going?\"}','2026-07-02 08:33:12'),(163,110,1,'Hi! It’s really nice to meet you — and I’m doing great, thanks for asking! 😊  \nSo, what’s your name, and what do you do when you’re not practicing English?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 08:33:13'),(164,110,2,'you','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 2, \"value\": 8.6, \"detail\": \"9 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 42, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"单个单词 \'You\' 本身没有语法错误，但作为独立句子不完整；建议补充上下文，例如 \'You are welcome\' 或 \'You did a great job\'。\", \"注意英文句子首字母必须大写，所以 \'you\' 应改为 \'You\'。\", \"B1 学习者应练习写出完整句子（主语 + 谓语），避免只用代词或孤立单词表达意思。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"You\", \"polished_version\": \"You\"}','2026-07-02 08:33:40'),(165,110,2,'Oh, you’re being playful — I love that! 😄  \nBut seriously — I’m Alex, and I help people practice everyday English. Now I’m curious: what’s your name, and what kind of work or studies keep you busy?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 08:33:41'),(166,110,3,'ლლლლლლლლლ Hi, I\'m so happy to chat with you. How are you?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 5, \"value\": 19.2, \"detail\": \"19 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 45, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 1 次 (1.6次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 1, \"pauses_per_min\": 1.6}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"ლლლლლლლლლ\", \"correction\": \"\", \"error_type\": \"other\", \"explanation\": \"这是格鲁吉亚字母（ Georgian script），不属于英语，属于乱码或误输入，必须删除才能使句子符合英语规范。\"}, {\"original\": \"I\'m so happy to chat with you.\", \"correction\": \"I\'m so happy to chat with you.\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"虽然语法正确，但‘so happy’在非正式问候中略显夸张；B1学习者更宜用自然、适度的表达（如‘great to’或‘pleased to’），避免过度情感强度导致语用不当。\"}, {\"original\": \"How are you?\", \"correction\": \"How are you?\", \"error_type\": \"word_order\", \"explanation\": \"该句本身无语法错误，但作为独立问候句，缺少连接词或上下文衔接时显得突兀；B1学生常忽略语境连贯性，此处虽非严格语法错误，但在真实交际中属常见语用疏漏（归类为word_order相关语序/衔接问题）\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"问候语尽量简洁自然：用 \'Hi there!\' 或 \'Hey!\' 比重复感叹更地道；\", \"避免过度使用 \'so + 形容词\'（如 so happy），B1阶段建议多用 \'really\', \'quite\', 或 \'great/lovely/nice to...\' 等更稳妥的表达；\", \"学会用破折号（—）或逗号连接两个短句，让对话更流畅，比如 \'...with you — how are you doing?\';\", \"‘How are you doing?’ 比 ‘How are you?’ 更常用于轻松聊天场景，听起来更友好、不生硬。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Hi, I\'m so happy to chat with you. How are you?\", \"polished_version\": \"Hi there! It\'s great to chat with you — how are you doing?\"}','2026-07-02 08:34:49'),(167,110,3,'Hi again — and wow, that’s a cheerful “ლლლლლლლლლ”! 😄  \nI’m doing well, thanks — and I’m really glad you’re excited to chat! So, what’s your name, and what do you enjoy doing in your free time?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 08:34:50'),(168,113,1,'Let\'s start with something simple. How\'s your day going so far?','user',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"注意 \'How\'s your day going?\' 是完全正确的现在进行时，用于询问当前正在进行的状态，没有语法错误；B1学生常误以为 \'going\' 需要改成过去式，但这里表达的是‘到目前为止的体验’，用现在进行时很自然\", \"‘so far’ 通常与现在完成时（如 ‘has been’）搭配更强调从过去到现在的时间段，因此 ‘How\'s your day been so far?’ 更地道、更 common in casual speech\", \"‘begin’ 和 ‘start’ 都正确，但 ‘begin’ 稍正式一点，和 ‘easy’ 搭配读起来更顺口，避免重复使用简单词（simple → easy）提升表达多样性\", \"记住：口语中 ‘How’s…?’ 是 ‘How has…?’ 的缩略，主语 + has/have + 过去分词 是现在完成时的标准结构；多听母语者说 ‘How’s it been?’ 来培养语感\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Let\'s start with something simple. How\'s your day going so far?\", \"polished_version\": \"Let\'s begin with something easy. How\'s your day been so far?\"}','2026-07-02 08:41:51'),(169,113,1,'It’s been lovely, thanks — busy but in a good way!  \nHow about you? Settling in okay? 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 08:41:52'),(170,113,2,'Thank you.','user',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"‘Thank you.’ 本身语法完全正确，没有错误——它是一个固定表达，常用于正式或 polite 场景。\", \"在日常对话中，B1 学习者可以尝试更自然的变体，如 ‘Thanks a lot!’ 或 ‘I really appreciate it!’ 来增强语气和亲和力。\", \"注意：句末用句号（.）是正确的；若想表达更热情，也可用感叹号（!），但需根据语境判断。\", \"避免过度修改正确句子——先确认是否真有错误，再练习替换为更地道的说法。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Thank you.\", \"polished_version\": \"Thanks a lot!\"}','2026-07-02 08:42:14'),(171,113,2,'You\'re very welcome!  \nShall I grab you a menu, or would you like to hear about today’s specials first?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 08:42:15'),(172,113,3,'ლლლლლლ','user',NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"errors\": [], \"suggestions\": [\"请提供一段有意义的英文句子，以便我帮您分析语法错误。当前输入 \'ლლლლლლ\' 是格鲁吉亚字母，不属于英语，无法进行英语语法分析。\", \"下次练习时，您可以写一个简单的英文句子（例如：\'She go to school yesterday.\'），我会帮您指出错误并解释原因。\", \"记住：英语语法分析需要真实、可识别的英文单词和结构——乱码或非拉丁字符不在分析范围内。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"\", \"polished_version\": \"\"}','2026-07-02 08:43:16'),(173,113,3,'Oh — looks like some keys got stuck! 😅  \nWould you like me to bring the menu, or shall I tell you about today’s specials?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 08:43:17'),(174,114,1,'Hi, I\'m so happy to talk to you. How are you?','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 13, \"value\": 50.7, \"detail\": \"51 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 53, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 08:50:40'),(175,114,1,'Hi! I’m really glad to meet you too — and I’m doing great, thanks for asking! 😊  \nSo, what’s your name, and what do you like to do in your free time?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 08:50:41'),(176,114,2,'Hmm.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 9, \"value\": 35.1, \"detail\": \"35 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 49, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 08:51:03'),(177,114,2,'No worries — take your time! 😊  \nHow about this: what’s something that always makes you smile — maybe a 