e\": \"plural\", \"explanation\": \"some 后接可数名词时，名词必须用复数形式；apple 是可数名词，泛指‘一些苹果’应说 apples\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"记住常见不规则动词的过去式（如 go→went, buy→bought），不要直接加 -ed\", \"注意 some 修饰可数名词时，名词一定要用复数；修饰不可数名词（如 water）才用单数\", \"多积累日常短语动词（phrasal verbs），比如 pop into（顺便进入）、pick up（顺便买），让表达更自然地道\", \"写完句子后，养成检查时间状语（如 yesterday）是否与动词时态一致的习惯\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I went to the store yesterday and bought some apples.\", \"polished_version\": \"I popped into the store yesterday and picked up some apples.\"}','2026-07-02 09:20:24'),(199,120,1,'Nice try! Just a small correction: *“I went to the store yesterday and bought some apples.”*  \nWould you like to tell me more — like what kind of apples you like, or why you went to the store? 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 09:20:25'),(200,120,2,'She have three childs and two mouses.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 13, \"value\": 224.8, \"detail\": \"225 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 53, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"have\", \"correction\": \"has\", \"error_type\": \"subject_verb_agreement\", \"explanation\": \"主语 \'She\' 是第三人称单数，动词必须用 has，不能用 have。\"}, {\"original\": \"childs\", \"correction\": \"children\", \"error_type\": \"plural\", \"explanation\": \"\'child\' 的复数形式是不规则变化 children，不是加 -s 的 childs。\"}, {\"original\": \"mouses\", \"correction\": \"mice\", \"error_type\": \"plural\", \"explanation\": \"\'mouse\'（老鼠）的复数形式是不规则变化 mice，不是加 -s 的 mouses（注意：computer mouse 的复数可为 mouses，但此处指动物，必须用 mice）。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"记住常见不规则名词复数：child → children，mouse → mice，foot → feet 等。\", \"第三人称单数主语（he/she/it）后，一般现在时动词要加 -s 或 -es（如 has, goes, watches）。\", \"口语中 \'She’s got...\' 比 \'She has...\' 更自然；\'kids\' 比 \'children\' 更常用在非正式场合。\", \"注意一词多义：\'mouse\' 指动物时复数是 mice，指电脑鼠标时复数可为 mouses —— 根据上下文判断。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"She has three children and two mice.\", \"polished_version\": \"She’s got three kids and two pet mice.\"}','2026-07-02 09:20:32'),(201,120,2,'Good effort! Here\'s a gentle correction: *“She has three children and two mice.”*  \n(“Children” and “mice” are the plural forms — they don’t follow the usual -s rule!)  \nBy the way, does she keep the mice as pets? Or is she a scientist? 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 09:20:35'),(202,121,1,'I go to the store yesterday and buy some apple.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 12, \"value\": 244.4, \"detail\": \"244 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 52, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"go\", \"correction\": \"went\", \"error_type\": \"tense\", \"explanation\": \"句子描述的是昨天发生的事，必须用一般过去时；go 是不规则动词，过去式是 went，不是 go 或 goed。\"}, {\"original\": \"buy\", \"correction\": \"bought\", \"error_type\": \"tense\", \"explanation\": \"and 连接两个并列谓语动词，时态需一致；前一个动词用了过去式 went，后一个也必须用过去式 bought。\"}, {\"original\": \"apple\", \"correction\": \"apples\", \"error_type\": \"plural\", \"explanation\": \"some 表示‘一些’，后面接可数名词时必须用复数形式；apple 是可数名词，所以应为 apples。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"记住常见不规则动词的过去式（如 go → went, buy → bought），不要按规则加 -ed。\", \"注意并列句中动词时态要保持一致：如果第一个动词是过去式，第二个也必须是过去式。\", \"some 后接可数名词复数（如 apples）或不可数名词（如 milk）；单数可数名词前不能直接用 some。\", \"尝试用更自然的短语替代基础表达，比如 \'pop into\'（顺便走进）、\'pick up\'（顺手买），让语言更地道。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I went to the store yesterday and bought some apples.\", \"polished_version\": \"I popped into the store yesterday and picked up some apples.\"}','2026-07-02 09:20:42'),(203,121,2,'She have three childs and two mouses.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 13, \"value\": 224.8, \"detail\": \"225 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 53, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"have\", \"correction\": \"has\", \"error_type\": \"subject_verb_agreement\", \"explanation\": \"主语 \'She\' 是第三人称单数，动词必须用 has，不能用 have\"}, {\"original\": \"childs\", \"correction\": \"children\", \"error_type\": \"plural\", \"explanation\": \"\'child\' 的复数形式是不规则变化 children，不是加 -s\"}, {\"original\": \"mouses\", \"correction\": \"mice\", \"error_type\": \"plural\", \"explanation\": \"\'mouse\'（动物）的复数形式是不规则变化 mice，不是加 -s\"}, {\"original\": \"She have\", \"correction\": \"She has\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"此处需要动词 \'have\' 的正确形式，但更准确地说，\'have\' 作为实义动词时，第三人称单数必须变为 \'has\' — 属于基本词汇形式误用\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"记住常见不规则名词复数：child → children，mouse → mice，foot → feet 等\", \"第三人称单数主语（he/she/it）后，一般现在时动词要加 -s 或用 has，比如 \'She has\', \'He likes\'\", \"口语中 \'She’s got...\' 比 \'She has...\' 更自然；\'kids\' 比 \'children\' 更常用在非正式场合\", \"注意区分 mouse（老鼠）和 mouse（鼠标）——后者复数可加 -s（mouses），但本句指动物，必须用 mice\"], \"corrected_text\": \"She has three children and two mice.\", \"polished_version\": \"She’s got three kids and two pet mice.\"}','2026-07-02 09:20:45'),(204,121,2,'Nice try! Just a small correction: *“I went to the store yesterday and bought some apples.”*  \nWould you like to tell me what kind of apples you like — or what else you usually pick up at the store? 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 09:20:46'),(205,121,2,'Thanks for sharing! Just a quick note — we usually say “went to the store yesterday and bought some apples” (since it’s past tense), and “She has three children and two mice.” 😊  \nWould you like to tell me a little about your family or what you enjoy doing in your free time?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 09:20:47'),(206,122,1,'I go to the store yesterday and buy some apple.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 12, \"value\": 244.4, \"detail\": \"244 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 52, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"go\", \"correction\": \"went\", \"error_type\": \"tense\", \"explanation\": \"句子中有时间状语 \'yesterday\'，表示过去发生的事，动词必须用过去式；\'go\' 是不规则动词，过去式是 \'went\'，不是 \'goed\'。\"}, {\"original\": \"buy\", \"correction\": \"bought\", \"error_type\": \"tense\", \"explanation\": \"并列谓语动词需与前一个动词时态一致；\'went\' 是过去式，所以 \'buy\' 也必须用过去式 \'bought\'。\"}, {\"original\": \"apple\", \"correction\": \"apples\", \"error_type\": \"plural\", \"explanation\": \"\'some\' 后接可数名词时，该名词必须用复数形式；\'apple\' 是可数名词，泛指‘一些苹果’应说 \'apples\'。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"记住常见不规则动词的过去式（如 go→went, buy→bought），不要按规则加 -ed。\", \"注意时间状语（如 yesterday, last week）是判断一般过去时的重要信号。\", \"使用 \'some\' 时要区分：后接不可数名词（如 some milk）用原形；后接可数名词（如 some apples）必须用复数。\", \"想让表达更自然，可以学几个常用口语化短语动词，比如 \'pop into\'（顺便进入）、\'pick up\'（顺手买下）。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"I went to the store yesterday and bought some apples.\", \"polished_version\": \"I popped into the store yesterday and picked up some apples.\"}','2026-07-02 09:20:55'),(207,122,2,'She have three childs and two mouses.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 13, \"value\": 224.8, \"detail\": \"225 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 53, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"have\", \"correction\": \"has\", \"error_type\": \"subject_verb_agreement\", \"explanation\": \"主语 \'She\' 是第三人称单数，动词需用 has，而不是 have。\"}, {\"original\": \"childs\", \"correction\": \"children\", \"error_type\": \"plural\", \"explanation\": \"\'child\' 的复数形式是不规则变化 children，不是加 -s 的 childs。\"}, {\"original\": \"mouses\", \"correction\": \"mice\", \"error_type\": \"plural\", \"explanation\": \"\'mouse\'（动物）的复数形式是不规则变化 mice，不是加 -s 的 mouses（注意：computer mouse 的复数有时用 mouses，但此处指动物，必须用 mice）。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"记住常见不规则名词复数：child → children，mouse → mice，foot → feet 等。\", \"第三人称单数主语（he/she/it）后，一般现在时动词要加 -s 或 -es（如 has, goes, watches），但 be 动词用 is。\", \"口语中 \'She’s got...\' 比 \'She has...\' 更自然；\'kids\' 比 \'children\' 更常用在非正式场合。\", \"注意区分同形异义词：mouse（老鼠）复数是 mice，而 mouse（鼠标）复数在技术语境中可说 mouses，但日常指动物时永远用 mice。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"She has three children and two mice.\", \"polished_version\": \"She’s got three kids and two pet mice.\"}','2026-07-02 09:20:58'),(208,122,3,'Okay, don\'t flex about that.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 14, \"value\": 221.2, \"detail\": \"221 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 54, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,'{\"errors\": [{\"original\": \"flex\", \"correction\": \"brag\", \"error_type\": \"word_choice\", \"explanation\": \"‘Flex’ 是非正式美式俚语（源自 ‘flex muscles’），虽在年轻人网络用语中表示‘炫耀’，但在标准B1英语教学中属于超纲词汇；‘brag’ 更准确、通用且符合中级学习者词汇范围。\"}, {\"original\": \"don\'t flex\", \"correction\": \"don’t brag\", \"error_type\": \"other\", \"explanation\": \"‘Don’t’ 后接动词原形，语法结构正确，但‘flex’作为动词在此语境下搭配不当且不自然——‘flex about something’ 不是惯用搭配；标准搭配是 ‘brag about something’ 或 ‘show off about something’。\"}], \"suggestions\": [\"B1阶段优先掌握常用动词如 brag, show off, boast，而非俚语 flex；它们更易理解且适用于考试和日常交流。\", \"注意动词与介词的固定搭配：brag *about* something, show off *about* something — 介词不能随意替换。\", \"‘Come on, no need to…’ 是更自然、语气更友善的表达方式，比直译‘Okay, don’t…’更符合英语母语者的日常习惯。\", \"避免过度使用缩写形式（如 don’t）在正式写作中；但在口语和非正式对话中可接受，需根据语境判断。\"], \"corrected_text\": \"Okay, don’t brag about that.\", \"polished_version\": \"Come on, no need to show off about that!\"}','2026-07-02 09:21:00'),(209,122,3,'Nice try! Just a small correction: *“I went to the store yesterday and bought some apples.”*  \nWould you like to tell me what kind of apples you like—or maybe what you usually buy at the store? 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 09:21:01'),(210,122,3,'No worries — we’re all learning! 😊  \nWould you like to practice correcting those sentences together? Or shall we move on to something else — like what you enjoy doing in your free time?','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 09:21:02'),(211,122,3,'Thanks for sharing! Just a quick note — we usually say “went to the store yesterday and bought some apples” (past tense for both verbs, and “apples” is plural since you’re talking about more than one). Also, “She has three children and two mice” — “children” and “mice” are the correct plural forms. Would you like to try rephrasing that sentence? I’m happy to help! 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 09:21:02'),(212,123,1,'Hmm.','user',NULL,'{\"wpm\": {\"max\": 25, \"label\": \"语速\", \"score\": 8, \"value\": 33.0, \"detail\": \"33 词/分钟\"}, \"overall\": 48, \"repetition\": {\"max\": 20, \"rate\": 0.0, \"label\": \"表达流畅度\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"重复率 0%\"}, \"pause_frequency\": {\"max\": 20, \"label\": \"停顿控制\", \"score\": 20, \"detail\": \"停顿 0 次 (0.0次/分钟)\", \"pause_count\": 0, \"pauses_per_min\": 0.0}}',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 09:24:35'),(213,123,1,'No worries — take your time! Maybe you\'d like to start with just your name? Or if you\'d rather, we can jump straight to something fun — like what you enjoy doing in your free time. 😊','assistant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-02 09:24:37'),(214,123,2,'Hi, I\'m